# LunaRec .gitignore
#
# Save this file as  LunaRec\.gitignore  (note the leading dot, no extension).
#
# Rule of thumb: commit what you WROTE, not what you DOWNLOADED or GENERATED.
# Source data is ~16 GB and is redistributable from ISRO PRADAN; derived
# rasters are regenerated by clip_dem.py. Neither belongs in version control,
# and GitHub rejects anything over 100 MB regardless.

# --- delivered PDS products: 16 GB, re-downloadable from PRADAN -------------
data/raw/

# --- derived rasters: regenerate with src/clip_dem.py -----------------------
*.tif
*.img
*.IMG

# --- patch files -----------------------------------------------------------
# The four current ones are ~550 KB each and ARE worth committing: every result
# in results/ was produced from exactly these, and without them the numbers
# cannot be reproduced. The superseded generations are not.
data/patches/superseded/

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- os / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.log
scratch/
